    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4",
        "note": "The statements use Freiman isomorphisms (IsAddFreimanIso), Module.finrank, vectorSpan, kernels of linear maps, the clique and independence numbers of a simple graph and the Cayley graph SimpleGraph.addCayley, which is the Cayley sum graph in F_2^n, from Mathlib. The proofs use its Freiman homomorphisms, affine independence, finite dimensional linear algebra and the Plünnecke–Ruzsa inequality, which is Theorem 24 of the paper and is used for Lemma 25. Mathlib has no restricted sumset, no Cayley sum graph, no space of Freiman homomorphisms and none of the results of the paper.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/gdahia/SumOfSetsInSeveralDimensions",
        "note": "A Lake dependency. It provides the affine dimension of a finite set (Finset.affineDim), Freiman's definition of the Freiman dimension (freimanDim), which Corollary 14 compares with Green's, and Freiman's lemma |A + A| ≥ (d + 1)|A| - d(d + 1)/2, from which Lemma 21 is proved.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      }
    ],
